# Godot 4 local cache/import artifacts — regenerated on open, not source.
.godot/
*.translation

# export_presets.cfg IS committed, deliberately — the usual Godot .gitignore
# excludes it (it can hold signing keystore paths and passwords) and that is why
# this project had no export configuration at all: nobody could tell whether it
# had never been written or had merely been ignored, and the game could not be
# built by anyone who cloned it.
#
# Ours holds no secrets: codesigning is off on every preset and there are no
# keystore paths. If signing is ever set up, move the secret parts to a
# credentials override rather than re-ignoring this file — the build config
# belongs with the build.

# Godot re-creates .import sidecars for anything dropped in assets/;
# they're machine-generated, not source. (The audio ones only appeared the
# first time an export ran the import pass — same class of file, same call.)
assets/**/*.import

# .uid sidecars, likewise. Godot 4.4+ suggests committing these; this project
# does not, because its .tscn files reference scripts by PATH rather than by
# uid:// (see any scene's ExtResource line), so nothing here depends on them
# and a fresh clone regenerates them. Keeping them out preserves the property
# tests/test_boot.gd and the README both rely on: clone, run, green, with no
# editor-generated file in the way.
*.uid
build_stamp.cfg
